Unique "electronic gift certificate" in the return goods Setouchi City added by hometown tax payment: Sanyo Shimbun Digital|San Deji
An electronic gift certificate "e-town gift".
Contact the dedicated equipment and make a payment.
On the 27th, Setouchi City announced on the 27th that it will add its own electronic gift certificate "emachi gift" to the return gift of the hometown tax payment.
It can be used at member stores in the city from November.
For the first time in the local government.
If you make a hometown tax payment and choose an electronic gift certificate as a return gift, the equivalent of thirty percent of the donation amount will be sent to the designated smartphone.
At the time of product purchase, the product ticket screen is displayed, and the store side contacts the dedicated equipment of the stamp type and settles it.
It cannot be transferred or re-sold.
Returns usually require a certain amount of time from application to arrival, but electronic gift vouchers can be received in an instant.
It can be easily used by tourists.
In addition to the five hometown tax payment portal sites, it is also accepted on the city's two special websites.
There are currently thirteen member stores, and by the end of this fiscal year we are aiming for one hundred stores.
In June, the Ministry of Internal Affairs and Communications established a new system that regulates local products, in order to prevent excessive competition among local governments.
According to the city, the city plans to "rote companies that deal with local products at participating stores, etc., within the scope of the guidelines."
Setouchi City's hometown tax payment for the 18th fiscal year is about four hundred and thirty million yen.
