South Korea-Bulgaria-Bulgaria summit to discuss measures to expand cooperation such as nuclear power and the defense industry (Yonhap News) - Yahoo! News
SEOUL (Reuters) - South Korean President Moon Jae-in held a meeting with Bulgarian Prime Minister Borissov, who is on an official visit to South Korea on Monday, in Cheongwadae (president's office) to discuss plans to expand substantive cooperation between the two countries.
This is the first visit of the Bulgarian Prime Minister.
President Moon welcomed Prime Minister Bolysov's visit to South Korea ahead of the 30th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations next year, and highly appreciated Prime Minister Borisov's leadership as a leader in Bulgaria's development.
The two leaders appreciated that trade and investment between the two countries continues to increase as trade protectionism expands globally, and agreed to work together so that economic cooperation will continue to expand.
President Moon welcomed Bulgaria's policy of granting South Korean companies a "strategic investor" and said they hope that it will promote Korean companies' investments in Bulgaria based on this.
He also stressed that while Bulgaria is promoting the introduction and modernization of its national defense, South Korea can become an optimal partner for Bulgaria, and called for interest and cooperation so that South Korean companies can participate in the Bulgarian government’s ordering of nuclear power plants and the promotion of the defense industry.
In addition, the two leaders agreed to strengthen futuristic forward-looking cooperation in electric vehicles (EVs) in the battery and automobile parts field and in the renewable energy sector.
Prime Minister Borisov expressed hope that close cooperation would be carried out in the fields of science, technology, and education with information and communication technology (ICT) led by South Korea.
They also discussed the peace process on the Korean Peninsula, and President Moon expressed his gratitude to the South Korean government's support of the efforts of the South Korean government to establish peace on the Korean Peninsula, such as making a statement in support of the inter-Korean and U.S.-North Korea summit.
Prime Minister Borissov reiterated President Moon’s willingness to build a peace regime on the Korean Peninsula and the South Korean government’s efforts, and reiterated the Bulgarian government’s firm support.
The meeting was also attended by Sung Yoon-mo, Secretary-General of the Ministry of Industry, Trade and Industry, Lee Ho-sung, Secretary-General of the Ministry of Industry, Trade and Industry; Lee Ho-sung, Chief of the Cheongwadae (president's office), and Kim Hyun-jeong, deputy head of the National Security Office.
Cho Se-yo-young, the first deputy secretary of the same department, also attended the meeting on behalf of Kang Kyung-hwa's foreign affairs minister during his visit to the United States.
Kinki Ceramics, which manufactures "Awaji-gawagara", a local industry in Hyogo and Awaji Island, filed for quasi-self-insolvency (Imperial Data Bank) (Imperial Data Bank) - Yahoo! News
Due to the slump in the housing market and the repeated damage caused by the earthquake disaster, "consumer's tile roof separation" also had an impact.
Kinki Ceramics Co., Ltd. (TDB company code: 530173983, capital: 992 million yen, 881-8 Otani, Awaji City, Hyogo Prefecture, representative Kozo Fukuhara, 44 employees) filed for self-insolvency with the Kobe District Court on August 30.
Daichi Yoshida (1-10-8 Nishi-Tenma, Kita-ku, Kita-ku, Osaka-ku, Osaka; Yoshida Daichi Law Office, Tel: +81-6-6365-6038).
Our company is a roof tile manufacturer, which was founded in 1895 and was restructured as a corporation in April 1961.
Initially, he started his business in Nishitan-cho, Mihara-gun (Minami-Awaji City) under the trade name of Kinki Kilnography Co., Ltd., as an Ibushi-ga tile manufacturer, which is a local industry on Awaji Island.
At the same time at the same time as the absorption-type merger of Kyowa Kiln Industry Co., Ltd. and the business of Kinki Sangyo Co.
After that, it opened sales offices in Fukuyama City, Hiroshima City, Oita City, Miyazaki City, etc., and it became the current system, and in the past it was mainly Ibushi tiles, but due to changes in consumer needs, Western tiles such as shiraita-gawara roof tiles were currently manufactured at a rate of seventy percent and Ibushi-gawara roof tiles at a rate of thirty percent.
We built a wide-ranging business base mainly in western Japan, such as major house manufacturers, building materials trading companies, and roof construction companies.
It was well-known as the top tile maker on Awaji Island.
Recently, however, due to the slump in the housing market after the Lehman shock, the Great East Japan Earthquake, the Great East Japan Earthquake and the Kumamoto earthquake, demand was sluggish due to sluggishness in consumer roofs.
In terms of earnings, in addition to a decline in profit margins associated with soaring fuel prices, the company was forced to face a severe financial position due to a series of losses due to the excess interest-bearing debt associated with inventory burdens and business fixed investment.
For this reason, financial institutions were trying to restructure their operations by requesting financial institutions to ease the repayment conditions for borrowings, but business conditions showed no signs of a recovery in business conditions, and their cash flow gradually tightened.
Unable to come and support us, we gave up on business continuity, and this was the measure.
The company’s debt is currently under investigation, but it is expected to be worth about two billion yen.
The Prefectural Dinosaur Museum in Katsuyama City, Fukui Prefecture promoting the "industrialization of tourism"
On the 25th of September, Katsuyama City in Fukui Prefecture announced a policy to acquire about 25300m2 of land adjacent to the construction site of the roadside station "Dinosaur Keiren Katsuyama", which will open next spring.
