<One year after the Eastern Iburi Earthquake> Securing water even in the event of a power outage Installation of a "sprisoning faucets" directly connected to the water pipe Hakodate's apartment: Hokkaido Shimbun Doshin electronic version
Countermeasures are being taken at an apartment building in Hakodate, where water was cut off in response to a blackout (black-out) due to a blackout (black-out) due to the Eastern Iburi Earthquake in September last year.
In the one year after the earthquake, seven condominiums have set up "snake fasceses" that can emit water even in the event of a power outage.
There are more than four-story condominiums and private-sector condominiums in the city, which have a "tank type" that may cut off water in the event of a power outage, and the department is calling for consideration of countermeasures.
There are two main water supply systems for a house: a water tank type in which water is deposited in a subterranean or on the roof, etc., and there are two types of "direct connection type" in which water is supplied directly to each house from the city's water distribution pipe.
Even if the water supply pipe is not damaged, if an electric pump that pulls up the water from the water tank into each house does not work due to a power outage, the water supply will not be able, and each house will run out of water.
