"The best director" (SPORT.es) - Yahoo! News
Jurgen Klopp, who won the best director award for "The Best," looks back on his career in an interview and has also left a comment on the status quo.
What surprised the public among his many remarks was about Manchester City manager Pep Guardiola's biggest rival in competing for a Premier League title.
Neymar’s best friend Avez said, “His happiness is still in Barça.”
“I couldn’t have imagined something so great. I’m very happy and I’m so proud of this award. It’s been a great few days for me. It’s been a great few days for me. Thanks to my players, I’ve been able to win this award. The most important thing is the team.”
Regarding Guardiola, Klopp said he “respects him very much,” adding: “What can I say about him? He’s won a lot of titles. His team’s style of playing is exceptional. He’s the best director I’ve ever played against, and it’s an honor to be nominated with him and to be able to compete for an award.”
He has also mentioned manager Pochettino and Tottenham.
“His last year was incredibly amazing. In many cases, if you don’t win a title, you won’t be in people’s memory. We were building a team little by little and we were playing in a great style.”
