[Rugby World Cup] one-shot exit & brawl U.S. player's "facial danger tackle" overseas ripples "insolent and despicable play" (THE ANSWER) - Yahoo! News
U.S.'s FL Quill makes rough-play, former England squad: 'It's not something you can call a tackle'
On the 26th of the Rugby World Cup (World Cup) in Japan, the U.S., which made its last appearance in the twenty participating countries, lost 7-45 to England.
It became a Kuroboshi departure, but the rough play played by FL John Quill in the second half is causing a ripple.
A one-shot exit in the form of adding a shoulder tackle to the opponent's face.
The actual scene was also released with a video in the overseas media, and the former England national team player also complained that it was "insulting and despicable play" and "it can not be called a tackle".
[Video] "Innocent and despicable play" and overseas ripples!
The actual moment of the "face danger tackle" played by the U.S. representative Quill
A warm battle has crossed the line.
It was the 29th minute of the 0-38 win.
Farrell, England's captain, was slightly out of balance when he caught an ally's pass.
It was Quill who went to the tackle for this.
However, he raised his upper body, not from the waist down, and hit his body violently on the upper body.
As a result, the other person's head and head come into contact, in the form of scratching the head.
Farrell fumbled violently and tumbled.
An Englishman protested against a play that clearly lacked legitimacy as he tried to push Quill away.
Players from the two armies gathered at once, and it became an instant air.
As a result of the TMO (video judgment), Quill was sent off with a red card.
Batsu left the pitch with a bad face, but the spectators who wanted fair play were also booed.
"Rugby's World Cup 2019: U.S. players are ejected with a despicable play, England is victorious."
"Kil made a despicable shoulder charge on Farrell's face and was sent off," the report said.
In the article, we introduced the comments of former England national team player and commentator Ugo Monya.
"It's insulting, it's despicable. You can't call it a tackle. It's a despicable play."
In the 81st minute, the U.S. somehow managed to escape a complete defeat with a nasty try in the 81st minute.
However, Quill's play left a bad aftertaste.
On September 26, the Ministry of Health, Labour and Welfare (MHLW) for the first time released the names of 424 hospitals judged to be "poor in clinical practice" among 1455 public hospitals and public hospitals such as JRCS nationwide.
In Fukui Prefecture, the Ministry of Health, Labour and Welfare verified the treatment results of fourteen public and public hospitals ▽ National Hospital Organization Awara Hospital▽Sakai Municipal Mikuni Hospital▽Oda Hospital in Echizen Town ▽ Wakasa Takahama Hospital in Takahama Town▽Four facilities were targeted.
⇒ Four hospitals subject to realignment "Cirtieth standards are crazy"
In order to suppress medical expenses that are expanding due to an aging population, it is necessary to promote reorganization and integration with hospitals in competing regions, so we decided to take an unusual response.
In October, we will request a full-scale review of the reorganization and integration at the target hospital, and we plan to reach a conclusion by September of next year.
There is no coercive force, but it is expected that there will be a backlash of local chiefs and residents due to concerns that there will be no familiar hospitals.
It was made public at a meeting on the same day.
The target hospitals accounted for 29 and 1% of the total, and there were many hospitals with a relatively small number of beds.
By prefecture, Niigata (53 and 7%), Hokkaido (48 and 6%), Miyagi (47 and 5 percent), Yamaguchi (46 and 7%) and Okayama (43 and 3%) were higher.
The number of targets was the highest in Hokkaido at fifty-four, and in Okinawa there was only zero.
Based on FY2017 data from FY2017, the Ministry of Health, Labour and Welfare conducted a survey of 1455hospitals in public and public hospitals that can respond to the “highly acute phase” for seriously ill patients and the “accurate phase” of performing general surgery.
Analysed the nine-item clinical record, such as cancer and emergency medical care, as well as whether a competing hospital is in a "twenty-two-minute-to-a-car" location, and judged the necessity of publicizing the hospital's name.
Eligible hospitals should consider abolishing it and transferring some departments to other hospitals.
The cost of health care soared in twenty-five years, for all baby boomers to be over seventy-five.
For this reason, the Ministry of Health, Labour and Welfare has set a goal of reducing the number of hospital beds with twelve-sixty-six-six-thirty-six-thousand-six-thousand-thousand-thousand-
At present, there are a large number of "high-accurate" and "accurate" beds in the "high-accurate" and "accurate phase" in which nurses are generously stationed, but there is a shortage for rehabilitations with high needs of the elderly.
In order to cope with the aging population, it is necessary not only to simply reduce the number of beds, but also to increase the focus on rehabilitation.
With regard to the reorganization and integration of hospitals, each prefecture has formulated a "regional medical care initiative" that stipulates the number of beds required in twenty-five years.
The entire country is divided into 339 districts, where local governments and medical personnel are discussing, but many local residents and chiefs have maintained a cautious stance, and the discussion has been troubling.
The Ministry of Health, Labour and Welfare wants to revitalize the discussion by publicizing the names of hospitals with a poor track record.
Komagadake Erupt Eruption Assumption, Comprehensive Disaster Prevention Training on the Road, etc. Wide area with the participation of the residents, for the first time in eighteen years (video) : Hokkaido Shimbun Doshin Electronic Version
A comprehensive disaster prevention drill assuming the eruption of Komagadake (1131m) was held on September 27th in Tori, Nanae, and Shikabe Town in Watarishima Kannai.
About four hundred people, including officials and residents of twenty institutions such as roads and three towns, participated.
It was held for the first time since the Hokkaido Komagadake Volcano Volcano Disaster Prevention Council in August formulated an evacuation plan that included evacuation routes for residents.
It is the first time in eighteen years that a wide-area training in which the population participates.
It is assumed that Mt.Komagatake had erupted at 8:45 a.m. and that mudslides had reached the town at the foot of the mountain.
When the eruption alert level was raised to five (evacuation), evacuation shelters were set up in forests and Nanae towns, and the residents moved by buses and roadside police vehicles prepared by each town.
