Climate demonstrations in Vancouver
The march took place from Vancouver City Hall, across Canbe Bridge, to a downtown library.
People with placards began to gather in front of the city hall of the meeting place a few hours before the start, and at the 13th time of the start time, there were enough people to fill the road in front of the city hall several blocks in front of the city hall.
After that, the number of participants continued to increase, and in the end, more than a hundred thousand people participated.
