A children's play facility and Minami-Numahara-ko, the outline of the construction will be decided Yamagata City|The Yamagata Shimbun
The successful bidder of a children's play facility and Minami-Numahara elementary school building, in which Yamagata City is proceeding with a construction plan using the social capital improvement (PFI) method using private funds, has been decided, and an explanation of the outline of the facility was explained at a meeting of the Standing Committee of the City Council held on the 26th.
An image of a children's amusement facility newly established in Kataya, Yamagata City
A children's play facility is planned to be built on the north side of Yamagata's Nakanaka in the Katayaji area.
The building is a one-story steel house with a total floor area of about three thousand square meters.
It is equipped with a semi-underground gymnasium, a cafe, and a book corner.
There will also be a universally-designed playground that children with disabilities can play outdoors, and three hundred parking spaces will be secured.
On the 5th of this month, a review committee was convened at the city hall, and a shelter group (Yamagata City), which consists of thirteen companies, sold it for three and a half million yen, including design, preparation costs, and maintenance and operation costs for fifteen years.
It is scheduled to start design and construction from January 2022 and open in March 2022.
Minami-Numahara Elementary School Building
Minami Numahara Elementary School is a large-scale school with more than nine hundred children.
It is planned to be built on the north side of the current school building in Iizawa City.
A three-story reinforced concrete building with a total floor area of about 8580 square meters.
There are two swimming pools, a steel-framed gymnasium and an after-school children's club.
On the 6th of this month's consideration committee, the Ichimura Corporation Group (Yamagata City), which is made up of eight companies, won the bid for four and a half million yen, including design, dismantling costs of the old school building, and maintenance and operation costs for fifteen years.
It began design and construction in December, and is scheduled to be completed in October.
