How to prevent dementia and limit it to the level of "forgotten things"?
Interview/Text/Watanabe Yo
Dementia drugs that major pharmaceutical companies and university hospitals are frustrated when they take on the challenge of research and development.
However, the relationship between dementia and lifestyle-related habits is being elucidated, and it has been found that there is a possibility that it is extremely mild and can be limited to the degree of forgetfulness.
We interviewed Professor Shunsuke Otsuki of the Stroke Center at Kinki University Hospital.
Dementia won't go away
Dementia prevention or treatment is long-awaited, but what is the current situation?
Ōtsuki Everyone may have dementia as they get older, regardless of the degree of difference, from mild to severe.
However, it is expected to take more than two decades for a new dementia drug to be developed.
Donepezil, which is often used in Japan, is already uninsured in some overseas countries, and it is not expected to have a pronounced complete healing effect.
On the other hand, while deaths due to infectious diseases and accidents are decreasing due to a decrease due to a decrease in the number of deaths due to the remarkable progress in treatment of anti-cancer drugs, people have been able to live a long life.
Therefore, it is also true that the number of patients with dementia is increasing.
It is necessary to create an environment in which society as a whole can live with peace of peace of mind in the local community, rather than being able to solve the problem not only by the person and
A way to “forgotten.”
Are there people who are more likely to have dementia or who are more likely to have dementia?
Otsuki Even if it is inevitable that you will have dementia, there is a possibility that the symptoms will be suppressed as much as possible, and it may be limited to the degree of “forgotten things”.
Dementia is considered as one of the lifestyle-related diseases, and there is a tendency for people who are prone to it.
First, people with metabolites are more likely to develop dementia.
Dementia is regarded as one of lifestyle-related diseases.
It is a combination of obesity, high blood pressure, diabetic and hypercholesterolemia.
The presence or absence of economic power will also have an impact.
For example, in the U.S., there are regions in the U.S. that distribute food vouchers called food vouchers to the poor, but the foods you can get with food vouchers are Frozen hamburgers, pizzas, and chicken that can be stored.
It can be used by people living in an environment where neither gas nor electricity can be used.
As a result, it becomes a diet low in vegetables and protein, and the lifestyle is biased towards lipids and sugar.
After a while, you will be poor but obese, and the only thing you have to do is to watch the TV and your body becomes unlucky.
A similar situation is possible in Japan.
In addition, people who do not think about things and do not work are more likely to have dementia.
In other words, in order to prevent dementia, it is necessary to read a book on a daily basis and think about things.
