State-of-the-art art that leads to another world Okayama art exchange opens in the city center: Sanyo Shimbun Digital|SANDIGI
People tour the classroom that became the stage of a video work that depicts the future three thousand years later = Former Uchi Yamashita Elementary School
On the 27th, an international art exhibition "Okayama Art Exchange 2019" (sponsored by an organizing committee created by the city, prefecture, etc.) held every three years held in the center of Okayama City opened on the 27th.
In line with the mysterious title "IF THE SNAKE, if the snake," art fans in Japan and overseas are enjoying the cutting-edge art created by eighteen artists from nine countries.
For the second time in sixteen years, the French artist Pierre Huyghe has been appointed as an artistic director to develop works that make use of Okayama's climate and local resources.
There will be about forty videos and three-dimensional works at thirteen locations, such as the former Uchiyamashita Elementary School (Marunouchi, Kita-ku, Okayama City) and the Tenjinyama Cultural Plaza (Tenjin-cho).
Prior to the opening ceremony, an opening ceremony was held at the same size, and about a hundred people from related parties attended.
Mayor Masao Omori and general producer Yasuharu Ishikawa, the chairman of the organizing committee, said, "Intellectual sensibilities are stimulated, and there are works where imagination and creativity can be stirred up. If it becomes an exhibition that attracts the attention of the whole world," and cut the tape.
Families and out-of-hospital school-educated children who visited the school quickly watched a snake-shaped robot that reacted to the sounds of the surroundings in the ring of the schoolyard and twitched their bodies, and toured the school building, which turned into the stage of a video work depicting the world three thousand years later.
I was enjoying the art in another world.
A 15-year-old high school freshman in Tokyo who is traveling with his father said, "The works that make use of the atmosphere of the old school building are interesting. It makes you imagine the time that flowed to this place."
It is closed until the 24th of November (the following day if it is a national holiday).
In Hong Kong, Umbrella Movement rallies in five years, tens of thousands, aiming for a general election|SHIZUOKA SHIMBUN AT-S
It’s been five years since the Umbrella Movement, and the people who gathered at the rally venue are in Hong Kong (Joint).
[Hong Kong Joint] On the 28th of the 5th and 28th of five years since the "Umbrella Movement", a large-scale demonstration calling for the democratization of Hong Kong's chief executive's election was held in a park near the Hong Kong government's headquarters building of Admirality (Kim Bell), where the demonstrators had the largest stronghold.
In the vicinity of the venue, some young people occupied the main road and threw flaming bottles at the government building.
In the midst of continued protests based on the proposed amendment to the Fugitive Offenders Ordinance, the participants renewed their determination to fight until the realization of a "true general election" that could not be won at that time.
Protests began in full-scale in June, more than the 79-day Umbrella Movement, and the demand for demonstrators has expanded to "five major demands" such as electoral system reforms.
